    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, keeping the given signature. Line net applies the line's own discount, then the 5% bulk discount for `standard` lines at qty 10 or more (multiplied, not added), then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Line tax is rounded per line from the region/category rate table. Totals, credit handling and `tax_by_rate` (with zero-rate lines included and unused rates omitted) are computed from those per-line values. Invalid region, category, qty (including `bool`), negative price or credit, and out-of-range discount all raise `ValueError`. I wrote 26 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering the rules, rounding edges, credit cases, and validation, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with 26 tests green. The one interpretation I made is that plain `int` or `str` values for money fields are converted to `Decimal` rather than rejected; the spec only says they are `Decimal`.",
